$ whycant read /etc/shadow

✗ alice (uid 1000) cannot read /etc/shadow

  /             drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /etc          drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /etc/shadow   -rw-r-----  root:shadow  ✗ read   ← blocked here

Why
  alice is not the owner (root) and is not in group "shadow",
  so the "other" permissions apply: ---. Reading a file needs r.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Grant read access only to alice via ACL:
       sudo setfacl -m u:alice:r /etc/shadow
  2. Add alice to the shadow group (log out and back in afterwards):
       sudo usermod -aG shadow alice
